--- uses: ["core"]
# Test that select-once correctly invokes the handler with a pre-seeded channel value
# and returns the handler result directly (not wrapped in Result.Ok after B-466).
#
# Strategy: send a value via an awaited task (forces the send before select-once polls),
# then call select-once and verify the handler result is returned directly.
# Only .result is accessed — the Channel value in ch is never serialized.
[
  ch:          [channel 1]
  send-done:   [await [task [fn [] [send ch 42]]]]
  ctx:         [context]
  source:      [ch: ch  handler: [fn [let x] [+ x 1]]]
  sources:     [seq source Seq.End]
  result:      [begin send-done [select-once ctx sources]]
]
.result
=== out
Int(43)
